 "open_points": [
  "The word list cannot read intent. Only the 8 mechanical clauses in 'clauses' are enforced by words; the other 12 need a reader, a systems gate or a picture check (see clauses).",
  "The slurs are not copied: slurs-v1.json stores them readable and unobfuscated, so the build reads that file itself (40 entries, word-bounded, case-insensitive). The C# rule 'slur' carries the same words as a regex; the browser build should load slurs-v1.json and build the pattern, so there is one list.",
  "Anachronism and real-brand lists are not in any gate today (the brand bible is the check for brands). The lists here are chosen starting lists, to be grown by the red-team set (RT-15, 300 lines).",
  "Rule 'drinking' and 'round' are broad and will catch harmless talk ('drinking' of tea); this follows the gate as built. A fallback line replaces the whole reply.",
  "COLLISION: the blueprint's firm term 'a round' (a set of payments collected, 2.17) is caught by rule aroundofdrinks ('a|your|my|his|her|their|our|whose|another|next round'). Prompts and the ui-text file avoid the word; a ruling is needed: rename the blueprint term (recommended: 'a collection') or whitelist it.",
  "ANACHRONISM SCOPE: the anachronism list applies to in-world speech, prompts and signs. Out-of-fiction screens (the AI notice, privacy page, credits, store text) must say 'internet' and are exempt from this category only (ui-text.json ai_notice, privacy, credits).",
  "Words such as 'child', 'kids', 'baby', 'pupil' also appear in the C# set as hard stops; the player's own typed input is NOT blocked by the gate, only answered in character (RT-15): see 'input_handling'.",
  "RECOMMENDED GATE CHANGE, 'a round': the patterns here stay exact to ContentWords.cs. Rule aroundofdrinks catches 'a round' and 'next round', which the blueprint uses for the firm's collection (2.17), and 'talk her round' style turns are a ruled mechanic. Recommend (1) rename the 2.17 term 'the collection' and (2) narrow the gate rule so talk, bring, come or turn + him, her, them + round is allowed. Needs his or the keeper's yes before the C# file is regenerated.",
  "RECOMMENDED GATE CHANGE, 'red light': rule prostitution matches red.?light, so 'a red light at speed' (driving, a junction) is blocked. Recommend narrowing to 'red-light (district|area|girls?)'.",
  "CASE: every pattern is case-insensitive except those with cased true (brandy and sherry, because Brandy and Sherry are names). Fallbacks and word lists below are matched case-insensitively and word-bounded.",
  "The prototype BANNED list (talk.js) had 'kiddies', 'the horses', 'internet', 'mobile phone' and 'email' which the C# list lacks: 'kiddies' is added to children and 'the horses' to gambling (chosen: true), and the other three are in anachronism."
 ],
